# When a key with an already-elapsed TTL is moved into place (SWAPDB) or created inside
# a MULTI while a client blocks on it, Redis propagates a DEL for the lazily-expired key.
# PeaDB's blocked-client wakeup path doesn't yet emit that DEL (expiry-propagation track,
# compat/delta.md item 15).
SWAPDB wants to wake blocked client, but the key already expired
