# Blocked-client "ready keys" serving order: a client already blocked on a key must be
# served before a later same-batch pop takes the value. PeaDB's immediate synchronous
# pop doesn't yet defer to a ready-keys queue (compat/delta.md item 15, blocked-client
# fairness). The pop operations themselves are correct.
Unblock fairness is kept while pipelining
Unblock fairness is kept during nested unblock
Blocking command accounted only once in commandstats
Blocking command accounted only once in commandstats after timeout
